Total Amiga Assembler
---------------------
The examples on this disk are stored in two main directories 
with examples relating to (or taken from) the main text of 
'Total Amiga Assembler' being held within sub-directories
of the directory called ChapterExamples. Each chapter has 
its own sub-directory containing the source listings, runable 
code and other associated files. If the example is a runable 
program then both the source code and an assembled version 
will be given. The examples from chapter 21 all consist of
a number of related files and to avoid confusion these file
sets have been placed in two sub-directories (Chapter21 and
Chapter21_Flash). Document files for the examples have not
been provided since the examples are fully discussed within 
the book itself. 

A number of other pieces of code have been provided in the 
OtherExamples directory. These do have document files!

IMPORTANT: You should note that most early executable examples 
are CLI/Shell based and so they do NOT have a corresponding icon 
file. To run these programs you need to open a CLI/Shell window 
and execute them as you would any other CLI/Shell program, ie 
type their name. Later chapter examples have been linked with 
suitable start-up code and are therefore both CLI/Shell and 
WorkBench runable (icons have been provided). You will find 
more details about CLI/Shell versus WorkBench running, 
start-up code, and other things in the document file called 
'ImportantNotes'. Needless to say it is important for you 
to read this BEFORE assembling and running the disk examples!



